{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>רבות</b> (Many): This is the new song, and רבות is an adjective modifying נפלאותיך, in the manner of רבים כל רבים עמים." "<b>ומחשבותיך</b> (and Your thoughts): Your decrees." "<b>אלינו</b> (toward us): on our account, or it is as it sounds, and he said: אלינו, corresponding to אלהינו." "<b>אין ערוך אליך</b> (none can be compared to You): A person has no ability to compare them to You, and the end will prove it. And some say: that it is like יערך לה׳, and if so, it itself is the accounting of returning to Your wonders."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:21.473677261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}